{"name":"Adhesion","hex":"#9e9cab","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"adhesion","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The ability of a substance to stick to an unlike substance.","Persistent attachment or loyalty."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/adhesion"}],"entries":[{"title":"Adhesion","blocks":[{"text":"Adhesion is the tendency of dissimilar particles or surfaces to cling to one another."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Spider_web_Luc_Viatour.jpg/330px-Spider_web_Luc_Viatour.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adhesion","wikidata":"Q188666"},{"title":"Adhesion (medicine)","blocks":[{"text":"Adhesions are fibrous bands that form between tissues and organs, often as a result of irritation of internal surfaces during surgery, infections or trauma. They may be thought of as internal scar tissue that connect tissues not normally connected."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Adhesions.jpg/330px-Adhesions.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adhesion_(medicine)","wikidata":"Q1967871"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Lucas-test-1-propanol-2-propanol-2-metyl-2-propanol.jpg/500px-Lucas-test-1-propanol-2-propanol-2-metyl-2-propanol.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Lucas-test-1-propanol-2-propanol-2-metyl-2-propanol.jpg/1280px-Lucas-test-1-propanol-2-propanol-2-metyl-2-propanol.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Lucas-test-1-propanol-2-propanol-2-metyl-2-propanol.jpg/500px-Lucas-test-1-propanol-2-propanol-2-metyl-2-propanol.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_camp